  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\text{Under inversion at F, the incircle and nine-point circle map to parallel lines}",
    "plain": "The classical inversive proof of Feuerbach's theorem: inversion centered at the Feuerbach point sends both circles to parallel lines, from which external tangency of excircles follows.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Provides an elegant synthetic proof alternative to coordinate computation",
      "Illuminates the deep projective symmetry in Feuerbach's theorem",
      "The parallel lines picture makes the excircle tangency visually immediate"
    ]
  },
