    "progressSummary": "PROVED: Created FeuerbachsTheoremOQ05.lean with 10 theorems (0 sorries, 0 axioms). Defined Feuerbach point, proved it lies on both circles, proved Circle-to-Line theorem, proved image lines are parallel.",
    "builtItems": [
      "Triangle.feuerbachPoint: F = N + (R/2/d)*(I-N) where d = R/2 - r",
      "feuerbachPoint_on_ninePointCircle: dist2 N F = R/2",
      "feuerbachPoint_on_incircle: dist2 I F = r",
      "invertPoint: planar inversion O k P = O + k²/|OP|² * (P-O)",
      "circle_to_line: circle through O → image line 2(Q-O)·(C-O) = k²",
      "incircle_maps_to_line: 2(Q-F)·(I-F) = k²",
      "ninePointCircle_maps_to_line: 2(Q-F)·(N-F) = k²",
      "feuerbach_normals_proportional: N-F = -(R/r)*(I-F)",
      "feuerbach_inversive_parallel_lines: ∃ λ, N-F = λ*(I-F)"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Key identity: on circle through O, |P-O|² = 2(P-O)·(C-O); proved via linear_combination hPC - hOC",
      "Feuerbach point: F = N + (R/2/d)*(I-N); gives dist N-F = R/2/d*d = R/2 and dist I-F = r/d*d = r",
      "Real.sqrt_mul and Real.sqrt_sq extract scalar factor from sqrt(t²*s) = t*sqrt(s) for t ≥ 0",
      "feuerbach_incircle_distance gives dist2 N I = |R/2-r|; abs_of_pos gives = R/2-r when r < R/2"
    ],
